@prefix : <https://loom.ogbuji.net/tech/building-and-working-knowledge-graphs-with-onya-and-local-llms/#howto-generator-script-not-substitute> .
@prefix schema: <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

:ontology a schema:DefinedTermSet ;
    schema:name "Generator-script output is not a substitute for the full skills-contract check"@en ;
    schema:description "Caught 2026-08-01 on the Onya/local-LLMs KG generation task: relying on rdf-infographic-skill's bundled generate_infographic.py plus its own validate-harness-contract.py / validate-infographic.py as proof of compliance, instead of cross-checking the delivered HTML against full-skills-contract-always-applies.ttl directly. Result: FAQ accordion existed (that specific prior-corrected defect was NOT repeated) but the nav inactivity-fade timer (already documented at full-skills-contract-always-applies.ttl#step-navInactivityFadeRequired since 2026-07-23) was missing, plus an About-section and Markdown companion were skipped entirely, plus a new defect (alias-IRI duplication) was introduced that no existing rule covered."@en .

:step-scriptOutputStillNeedsManualChecklist a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    schema:name "Bundled generator scripts + their own validators check a NARROWER surface than the full contract — run the full-skills-contract-always-applies.ttl checklist manually against the output regardless of what the script's validator reports"@en ;
    schema:text "rdf-infographic-skill/scripts/generate_infographic.py auto-assembles HTML and runs validate-harness-contract.py (resolver hrefs, KG explorer edge anchors, SPARQL button) and validate-infographic.py (generic quality heuristics). Neither one checks: nav 2-minute inactivity fade, FAQ accordion functioning as a real toggle (vs. merely present), About-section presence, or Markdown-companion existence. A PASS from both scripts is necessary but not sufficient; before calling delivery done, grep the output HTML directly for each item in full-skills-contract-always-applies.ttl's step list (FAQ role=button + toggle JS, inactivity-fade IIFE, About section id, MD file existence) rather than trusting the script's own exit status."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : .

:step-synopsisAndHeroAttributionMissing a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 3 ;
    schema:name "generate_infographic.py renders People/Organizations/FAQ/Glossary/HowTo but never the article-level schema:abstract/schema:articleBody as a visible Synopsis section, and never a hero-meta 'KG curated by ... on behalf of Kingsley Idehen' attribution line — both must be added manually after generation"@en ;
    schema:text "Caught 2026-08-01, same task, after the first round of fixes: the reader asked 'where is the synopsis' and 'what happened to the hero attribution', surfacing two more gaps the generator's own validators do not check -- render the RDF's schema:abstract + schema:articleBody as a Synopsis section immediately after the hero, and add the standard hero-meta curated-by line plus matching JSON-LD accountablePerson/prov:actedOnBehalfOf triples, per kg-curation-attribution.ttl."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : .

:step-sectionBodyTextNeverRendered a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 4 ;
    schema:name "generate_infographic.py extracts People/Organizations/FAQ/Glossary/HowTo from the RDF but never renders schema:CreativeWork section entities' own schema:text as visible narrative prose — the article's actual walkthrough body is silently dropped"@en ;
    schema:text "Caught 2026-08-01, same task, after Synopsis/hero-attribution fixes: 11 schema:CreativeWork section entities (:sectionChallenge, :sectionSetup, etc.) each had full schema:text in the RDF, referenced via :article schema:hasPart, but none were ever rendered as HTML -- only a 2-paragraph Synopsis (abstract+articleBody) plus the entity-index sections existed, so every entity/citation mentioned only inside a section's narrative text (Laurent Picard's cited article title, the power-steering article, mlx-notes repo, Qwen model variants, Onya Literate, docheader, nodebase, merge(), betweenness/Louvain, 3SO) was entirely absent from visible prose, not merely unlinked. FIX: after generation, grep the RDF for every schema:CreativeWork under :article schema:hasPart and confirm each one's schema:text appears somewhere in the rendered HTML body -- not just as a kgData JSON node label."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : .

:step-kgExplorerBasicModeFeaturesIncomplete a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 5 ;
    schema:name "generate_infographic.py's KG Explorer omits several Basic-mode non-negotiables from SKILL.md: node label geometry/contrast, search, hover tooltip, predicate description mapping, and edge hover highlighting"@en ;
    schema:text "Caught 2026-08-01, same task: node labels used dx:15/dy:4 (beside the circle, no text-anchor, no paint-order contrast stroke) instead of the documented y=r+11 below-circle placement with paint-order:stroke + stroke:var(--bg); there was no #kgSearch input, no node hover tooltip, no PREDICATE_DESC mapping, and no edge mouseenter/mouseleave highlighting -- all explicitly required by SKILL.md's Basic Mode section and KG Explorer Non-Negotiables. The Advanced settings panel DID have working node-type/predicate filters, physics sliders, and resolver preference, so the gap is specifically the Basic-mode-visible feature set, not the whole explorer. FIX: after generation, diff the rendered KG Explorer toolbar against SKILL.md's Basic Mode bullet list item by item; do not assume a populated Advanced panel means Basic mode is also complete."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : .

:step-loadInBrowserNotJustGrep a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 6 ;
    schema:name "Static text/JS-syntax validation cannot catch a broken external script URL — an HTML+RDF infographic delivery MUST be loaded in an actual browser and checked for console errors and real DOM output before being called done"@en ;
    schema:text """Caught 2026-08-02, same task, after five separate 'PASS' validator runs and a `node --check` JS-syntax check: the KG Explorer's SVG was completely blank in a real browser the entire session, because the skill's own template (rdf-infographic-skill/scripts/templates/base_template.html) hard-codes `<script src="https://d3js.org/d3@7"></script>` -- a URL that returns HTTP 404 (the correct path is `https://d3js.org/d3.v7.min.js` or the jsdelivr equivalent used elsewhere in the same skill's rdf-to-kg-section.py). Because `window.d3` was `undefined`, `renderKG()`'s `if (!d3) return;` guard silently no-opped after appending only the arrow marker defs -- node/link COUNT badges still showed correct numbers (computed before the d3 check), so even a glance at the counts looked fine. This bug predates the current task entirely: it is in the skill's own template, so every prior infographic built with this generator has shipped with a non-functional KG Explorer, undetected, because:
  1. validate-harness-contract.py's own D3 check (`require(html, 'd3@7', ...)`) was checking for the LITERAL BROKEN STRING as proof of correctness -- it could never fail on this bug, only confirm the bug's presence. Fixed alongside this entry to require a working URL pattern via regex instead.
  2. `node --check` verifies JS syntax, not runtime behavior or external resource availability -- a syntactically perfect script that never executes (because its dependency 404s) passes silently.
  3. No prior delivery in this session loaded the actual HTML file in a browser and inspected the live DOM or console.

FIX (mandatory before declaring any HTML+RDF infographic delivery done): open the file in an actual browser (a local static server + this tool's browser pane, since `file://` URLs outside the project directory render as inert static snapshots), check `read_console_messages` for errors, and verify with `document.querySelectorAll('.node-group').length` / `.link-line` (or equivalent) that the graph actually populated -- not just that the count badges show non-zero text. Grep-based and syntax-only validation is a floor, not a ceiling; it cannot catch a dead external CDN URL, a silently-swallowed runtime guard, or any other failure that only manifests when the page actually executes."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : .

:step-aliasIriMustStayUntyped a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    schema:name "owl:sameAs alias IRIs (alternate platform identities) must NOT be re-typed as full entities (rdf:type + schema:name) — the RDF-to-HTML entity extractor treats every typed subject as a distinct card, causing visible duplication"@en ;
    schema:text "When a primary entity IRI (e.g. a person's LinkedIn profile) carries owl:sameAs links to alternate platform identities (X/Twitter, linktr.ee, a homepage), those alternate IRIs must be referenced ONLY as owl:sameAs objects -- do not also declare `a schema:Person`/`schema:Organization` plus `schema:name` on them. rdf-infographic-skill's RDF-to-HTML extraction (and any similar KG-explorer/People-section renderer) enumerates every subject with a matching rdf:type as its own card; it does not dedupe across owl:sameAs. Typing the aliases produces visible duplicate People/Organization cards for what is semantically one entity (caught 2026-08-01: Uche Ogbuji rendered 3x, Gordon Frickers 2x, Oori Data 2x, from LinkedIn+X+linktr.ee and DBpedia+homepage and homepage+LinkedIn-company pairs respectively; recurred 2026-08-09 on the Sangeet Paul Choudary/Reshuffle scarcity-and-strategy KG — X and Substack alias IRIs were typed `a schema:Person` with their own `schema:name`, rendering the person 3x in the People section; user caught it post-delivery by asking 'why the redundancy' rather than it being caught pre-delivery, since this exact rule already existed at generation time and was not applied). Fix: keep the primary (highest-priority-ladder) IRI as the sole typed, named entity; alias IRIs appear in the graph only as the object of owl:sameAs triples, with no other properties asserted on them, unless a genuine reason exists to describe them separately. Because this rule has now recurred 4 times across 2 sessions, treat it as a mandatory pre-delivery grep: after drafting any RDF with owl:sameAs, grep the file for every owl:sameAs object IRI and confirm none of them also appears as a subject with `a schema:`."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : .
